From c892cbd7f468a3598e899155a48812b892d86e87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:16:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ft_connectivity_psi: exclude the last frequency bin from the
 slope window

phaseslope overwrites x(1:end-1) with the products conj(C(f)).*C(f+df) but
leaves x(end) as the raw coherency at the highest frequency. Every window
that reaches the top bin (the last nbin+1 output bins) therefore adds
imag(C(fmax)) to the phase slope index. With normalize='yes' the situation
is worse: coh(end) stays 0, so x(end)./coh(end) is infinite and the last
nbin+1 bins of the PSI are -Inf/+Inf (verified with a 20-bin synthetic
coherency, nbin=3: bins 17..20 = -Inf).

Zero the last element after forming the products (and set its normalizer
to 1) so those windows simply contain one fewer product, which is the
behaviour of the Nolte et al. (2008) definition at the edge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012d2sJAD5EUp4GqAStqoBX7
---
 connectivity/ft_connectivity_psi.m | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/connectivity/ft_connectivity_psi.m b/connectivity/ft_connectivity_psi.m
index 2f5225e..2dada42 100644
--- a/connectivity/ft_connectivity_psi.m
+++ b/connectivity/ft_connectivity_psi.m
@@ -141,10 +141,14 @@ function [y] = phaseslope(x, n, norm)
 m   = size(x, 1); % total number of frequency bins
 y   = zeros(size(x));
 x(1:end-1,:,:,:,:) = conj(x(1:end-1,:,:,:,:)).*x(2:end,:,:,:,:);
+% the last element holds no product (there is no bin above it); zero it so
+% that windows reaching the highest bin do not add the raw coherency there
+x(end,:,:,:,:) = 0;
 
 if strcmp(norm, 'yes')
   coh = zeros(size(x));
   coh(1:end-1,:,:,:,:) = (abs(x(1:end-1,:,:,:,:)) .* abs(x(2:end,:,:,:,:))) + 1;
+  coh(end,:,:,:,:) = 1; % avoid 0/0 for the (zeroed) last element
   %FIXME why the +1? get the coherence
   for k = 1:m
     begindx = max(1,k-n);
